We can use the alembic revision command in conjunction with the --autogenerate option. 

<code>$ alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Added new table"<code>

Running the migration

<code>$ alembic upgrade head<code>

‘stamp’ the revision table with the given revision; don’t run any migrations.

<code>$ alembic stamp {head}<code>

**Use -x option after alembic command for specifiyng .env file path relative to src directory if any -> alembic -x env=../.env ...**